  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TDA Turkey</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">TDA Turkiet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den l&#xe5;ngsiktiga visionen f&#xf6;r TDA &#xe4;r ett demokratiskt, fritt och r&#xe4;ttvist Syrien med ett regeringssystem byggt av det syriska folket. Syriernas r&#xe4;ttigheter, fred, stabilitet, v&#xe4;lst&#xe5;nd, r&#xe4;ttvisa och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet kan endast uppn&#xe5;s genom en process av demokratisk &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ng och ett omfattande nationellt program f&#xf6;r &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsr&#xe4;ttvisa som l&#xe4;gger grunden f&#xf6;r r&#xe4;ttvisa och f&#xf6;rsoning.

De arbetar f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka det syriska civila samh&#xe4;llet, ta itu med effekterna av politisk och samh&#xe4;llelig auktoritarism, inklusive diskriminering av kvinnor och p&#xe5;verka beslutsfattare i en demokratisk &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ng och r&#xe4;ttvisa i Syrien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The long-term vision of TDA is: A democratic, free, and just Syria with a system of government built by the Syrian people. Syrians&#x2019; rights, peace, stability, prosperity, justice, and gender equality can only be achieved through a process of democratic transition and a comprehensive national program for transitional justice that lays the foundation for justice and reconciliation.

Their works serves to empowering Syrian civil society, addressing the impact of political and societal authoritarianism, including discrimination against women, and influencing decision-makers to serve democratic transition and justice in Syria.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Project is to establish a rights-based, inclusive, and accountable environment in Syria, advancing transitional justice, democratic participation, and the protection of HLP (Housing, Land and property) rights, thereby promoting the dignity and resilience of communities and individuals.</narrative>
  </description>
